    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d232">

                <pb facs="0296" n="284" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Japan)/8–1046: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Durbrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi><anchor n="60" xml:id="d232-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-10T16:00:00+03:00">August 10, 1946—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>Received August 10—1:21 p.m.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3156. Depcir August 8, noon.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d232-f2"/> Independent
                    attitude displayed by Soviet military in Japan seems to parallel behavior of
                    Soviet military representatives in Italy last year. Dept will recall that when
                    such behavior was brought to our attention we recommended in part that SACMED
                    take local military administrative action including detention of any Soviet
                    representatives who acted in unauthorized manner (Emb’s 3771, November 5,
                        1945<anchor n="62" xml:id="d232-f3"/>).</p>
                <p>Soviet Military authorities themselves strictly enforce security measures and
                    cannot logically object if we do same. So far as our view has a bearing on issue
                    we feel that SCAP would be justified in taking firm measures to keep Soviet
                    officers in bounds.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Durbrow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d232-f1" n="60" type="source" xml:id="d232-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated by the Department as telegram 452, August 16, 1946, 8 p.m., to the
                    Political Adviser in Japan.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d232-f2" n="61" xml:id="d232-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported telegram 351, August 1, 1946, from Tokyo, <ref
                        target="#pg280">p. 280</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d232-f3" n="62" xml:id="d232-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
